[4] Why does create2 predicted address not equal actual address? (cited)
Answers > Answer (score 1, accepted): For some reason the predicted/pre-computed address is not equal to the actual address when the created contract accepts address for it's constructor parameters, however it's fine when the constructor parameters are uint

That's because you are not using `abi.encode` on the arguments but `abi.encodePacked`. As `abi.encode` pads the elements to 32 bytes there is no difference if your parameters are already 32 bytes long, as uint. In the case of `address` the missing padding leads to different output.

A more generic and correct version would therefore be :

  address predictedAddress = address(uint160(uint(keccak256(abi.encodePacked(
        bytes1(0xff),
        address(this),
        salt,
        keccak256(abi.encodePacked(
            type(Test2).creationCode,
            abi.encode(address1, address2) // <-- abi.encode the parameters
        ))
    )))));

I managed to get it working, all I had to do was cast the address to uint

